<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44215" root="&#xA;                        نيل&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَالَ مِنْهُ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He defamed him.</i> (L, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قبح</span>.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَالَ مِنْ عِرْضِهِ</span>
                        <i>He defamed him.</i> (T, K, TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَال مِنْهُ</span>
                        <i>He harmed, hurt,</i> or <i>injured him,</i>
namely, an enemy. (Mgh.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَالَهُ بِلِسَانِهِ</span> is
coupled in the Msb, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قرص</span>, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَذَاهُ</span>; and
seems plainly to signify <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَصاَبَهُ</span>, which, in this
case, is the same as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَذَاهُ</span>. And ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنَاوَلَهُ</span></b>  has a
similar meaning. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَالَ</span>
                        <i>He obtained,</i> or <i>attained.</i>
(S, K.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَالَ مِنْ عَدُوِّهِ</span>
                        <i>He attained</i> [or <i>obtained</i>]
<i>the object of his aim,</i> or <i>desire, from his enemy.</i>
(Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b6-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَالَهُ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَنَالُ</span>, <i>It reached him; came
to him;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَصَلَ إِلَيْهِ</span>. (M, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نيل</span>.) See also
Bd, xxii. 38. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b7-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَالَ لَكَ أَنْ نَفْعَلَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَنِيلُ</span>;
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكَ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنَالَ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنَى</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b8-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَالَهُ</span>, first. pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِلْتَهُ</span>,
inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَيْلٌ</span>, <i>He obtained it; he attained it;</i>
namely, the object of his wish, &amp;c. (S, K,
Msb, &amp;c.)

